---
import Layout from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { base } from "../lib/site";
---
<Layout
  title="Research hub"
  description="Bibliography, evidence labels, and reading library for zhao-langxi HRI essays."
  canonical="https://zhao-langxi.github.io/zhao-langxi/research.html"
  current="research"
>
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <header>
      <p>Research and methods</p>
      <h1>Research hub</h1>
      <p>Parked with the essays. Digital Humans writing is on hiatus. Start with the labels if you still want to check a claim.</p>
    </header>
    <article>
      <ul class="resource-list">
        <li>
          <h2><a href={`${base}research/evidence-labels.html`}>Evidence labels</a></h2>
          <p>Read this first. It defines <strong>Observed</strong>, <strong>Reported</strong>, <strong>Interpreted</strong>, and <strong>Open question</strong>.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2><a href={`${base}research/bibliography.html`}>Open bibliography</a></h2>
          <p>EU AI Act, Hong Kong PCPD, mainland labelling rules, HRI interruption papers, and the public concierge coverage. Start here if you want to check a claim.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2><a href={`${base}research/reading-library.md`}>HRI reading library</a></h2>
          <p>Open robotics tools plus the same papers, grouped for later essays ... not a course syllabus.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Contributing references</h2>
      <p>
        Use GitHub Issues or a pull request that adds a row to <code>bibliography.md</code> with a stable link.
        Do not paste paywalled full text without permission.
      </p>
      <p><a href={base}>← Home</a></p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
